Here are the exact Excel formulas to calculate the **Calculated Weighted Score** in Column K. I have provided both a baseline formula and an advanced version that incorporates the evidence-gating logic discussed previously.

You will paste these into cell **K4** and drag them down to **K7**.

### Option 1: Baseline Weighted Override Formula

This formula executes the standard validation logic: it prioritizes the 2LoD verified score if one exists; if not, it uses the 1LoD self-assessment, multiplies it by the criticality weight, and explicitly handles "N/A" declarations to prevent math errors.

**Formula for K4:**

```excel
=IF(OR(UPPER(TRIM(F4))="N/A", UPPER(TRIM(J4))="N/A"), "N/A", E4 * IF(ISNUMBER(J4), J4, F4))

```

**Logic Breakdown:**

* **`IF(OR(UPPER(TRIM(F4))="N/A"...`**: Checks if either the 1LoD or 2LoD has declared the control "N/A". If true, it outputs "N/A" (text) so this row is excluded from domain-level averages.
* **`IF(ISNUMBER(J4), J4, F4)`**: The Authority Override. It checks if the 2LoD Verified column (J) contains a number. If 2LoD has audited and scored it, that score becomes the absolute truth. If J4 is blank, it defaults to the 1LoD score (F4).
* **`E4 *`**: Multiplies the final accepted maturity level (0-5) by the Control Criticality Weight (1-5) to generate the localized risk score.

