### Domain-Level Aggregation (The Heat Map Feeder)

Because you are outputting text ("N/A") for non-applicable controls, you cannot use a simple average formula at the bottom of the section. To calculate the final Domain Score (out of a maximum of 5) without penalizing the vendor for N/A controls, use this formula below your block of questions:

```excel
=SUMIF(K4:K7, "<>N/A") / SUMIF(K4:K7, "<>N/A", E4:E7)

```

**How the Aggregation Works:**

1. **`SUMIF(K4:K7, "<>N/A")`**: Adds up all the calculated weighted scores, ignoring any row marked "N/A".
2. **`SUMIF(K4:K7, "<>N/A", E4:E7)`**: Adds up the *weights* (Column E) only for the rows that were actually scored (ignoring the weights of N/A rows).
3. **The Division**: Divides the total weighted points by the total active weights, returning a mathematically pure Domain Score between 0.0 and 5.0.
